1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,000
===SCENE1===
Arjuna said, "O Krishna, I have heard that you are the one who is beyond human birth and death

2
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:23,000
You are the eternal and unchanging essence of all existence."

===SCENE2===
This verse means that Arjuna is acknowledging Krishna's divine nature and recognizing him as the ultimate reality.

===SCENE3===
In this deeper sense, Krishna's words remind us that we too can transcend our limited human identities and connect with the divine within ourselves

3
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:35,000
We must look beyond the surface level of our physical bodies and recognize the eternal essence that resides within each of us.

===SCENE4===
This verse teaches us the importance of self-realization and spiritual awareness

4
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:46,000
It encourages us to look beyond our egoistic tendencies and recognize our true nature as a spark of the divine

5
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:58,000
By doing so, we can transcend our limitations and experience a deeper sense of purpose and meaning in life.

